nend)\n","file":"tests/irinterp_spec.lua"}},"decisions":[],"bytes":4431,"decided_by":"tactic"},{"id":"1790869477.210262-edit","verb":"edit","invocation":{"touched":[".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"],"verb":"edit","args":{"before":"| Interpret a C function ABSTRACTLY for ANY library — which elements of a finite set (a slot's value x the frame's count) reach a return, which a no-return raiser, and the value returned — with no library name in the engine | `local CI = require 'cartograph.cinterp'` — `ctx = CI.units(sources)` (defs per unit, typedefs, enums over preprocessed `{ { name, text } }`), then the adapter adds `frame = { top, base, origin }` (fields of the thread), `layout` (the slot's), `reps` (each element's representative), `sentinels`, `noret`, `builtins`; `CI.analyzer(ctx).run(def, { CI.thread(), … , n }, slots, focus, { ['TAG@count'] = true … }, false)` → `{ ret, rej, vals, returns, over }` per element. An AGGREGATE passes BY VALUE (a 16-byte JSValue): a compound literal, positional or designated, nested ones flattened to member paths (`ctx.aggregates`, every struct / union typedef in declaration order), a field read back, a field write a functional update, two paths joined keeping the members they agree on; a representative of SEVERAL words (`reps.tag[t].words`) is read at the word its field lies in. Loops are fixpoints over `cfg.graph`; the frame's top / base are path values, its origin one value across reallocation. `CI.count()` as an argument is each element's own count (`TAG@count`); `ctx.throwers = { [name] = value }` makes a call that value without walking the body; `A.expr(text)` evaluates one expression of the tree (a sentinel, a pad); `A.self` keeps each callee's own steps and `A.toobig[id]` makes a callee an unknown call; a call DEPTH past 48 is an unknown call. An OUT-PARAMETER (`&local` handed to a callee) is a cell the callee's `*p` reads and writes, the caller's local after the call; a word handed to a POINTER parameter is